{
  "id": "lacp",
  "label": "LACP",
  "rfc": [],
  "notes": "Link Aggregation Control Protocol (IEEE 802.1AX) over the Slow Protocols EtherType 0x8809, sent to 01:80:c2:00:00:02. The Actor, Partner, Collector and Terminator TLVs are mandatory with fixed lengths, so the first 60 bytes of an LACPDU sit at fixed offsets and every field is modelled; the reserved runs inside the TLVs and the trailing 50 bytes of the 110-byte LACPDU are zero padding, modelled as exclusions. The Marker PDU shares the EtherType with subtype 2 and is not covered. PAgP, the Cisco counterpart, runs on a different EtherType and is out of scope.",
